{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2968","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2968","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2968\",\"parent_revision\":\"3d3307a7b52ca1605c5ad83dbdd9b8e166d4c5f791395556a2097d4727baeef4\",\"root_revision\":\"3d3307a7b52ca1605c5ad83dbdd9b8e166d4c5f791395556a2097d4727baeef4\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-18\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDiscovered via a hypothesis property test written while reworking #2956's fix (PR #2964), related to #2966 (Unicode title-casing round trip) but a distinct root cause.\\n\\nrendering.heading_to_unknown_key() encodes a section display name into a storage key by lowercasing and replacing every space with an underscore (\\\"Impact Radius\\\" -> \\\"unknown__impact_radius\\\"). This encoding is ambiguous/lossy for any display name that itself contains a literal underscore, or that (after ATX-heading whitespace normalization on re-parse) collapses to something indistinguishable from an underscore-only string.\\n\\nConcrete falsifying example: section_name = \\\"_\\\" (a single underscore).\\n- heading_to_unknown_key(\\\"_\\\") -> key = \\\"unknown___\\\" (three underscores: the \\\"unknown__\\\" prefix plus the literal \\\"_\\\").\\n- unknown_key_to_heading(\\\"unknown___\\\") -> strips the \\\"unknown__\\\" prefix, leaving \\\"_\\\" -> replace(\\\"_\\\", \\\" \\\") -> \\\" \\\" (a single space) -> .title() -> \\\" \\\" (unchanged). The heading text is now a single space.\\n- Rendered as \\\"##  \\\" (two spaces after the ATX marker). On re-parse, the ATX heading regex's \\\\s+ consumes all the whitespace, leaving an EMPTY heading name.\\n- Re-normalizing \\\"\\\" produces key \\\"unknown__\\\" (only the prefix, two underscores) -- different from the original \\\"unknown___\\\".\\n\\nImpact: narrow -- only affects section names that are literal underscores/whitespace-only after stripping, an unrealistic input for a human/agent-authored display name (no one names a section \\\"_\\\"). Confirmed distinct from #2966 (that one is a Unicode str.title() casing quirk; this one is the underscore-as-space-separator encoding itself being non-invertible for names containing literal underscores).\\n\\n**Research first**: a full fix likely requires either escaping literal underscores in the source name before substituting for spaces (so the two are distinguishable on the reverse transform), or storing the original display name verbatim instead of round-tripping it through a lossy encode/decode pair -- the same design question raised in #2966. Consider resolving both together.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **unknown-section key encoding conflates literal underscores in a section name with space-substitution underscores** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input, found via hypothesis property test written for #2956\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Investigation Update 2026 08 20\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Verdict: NOT RESOLVED.** Confirmed by direct execution against current `main`:\\n\\n```\\nheading_to_unknown_key('Foo_Bar') -> 'unknown__foo_bar'\\nheading_to_unknown_key('Foo Bar') -> 'unknown__foo_bar'   # COLLISION\\n```\\n\\nAlso confirmed `'Foo__Bar'` vs `'Foo  Bar'` (double underscore vs double space) collide identically, and this issue's own literal `\\\"_\\\"` example still collides with `\\\"\\\"` (both -> `unknown__`), just via a different path than originally described \u2014 the #2979 fix (`_NON_ALNUM_RE`) widened the punctuation-collapsing regex, which made the collision *more* general, not less, since the mapping was never injective.\\n\\n**Root cause**: `heading_to_unknown_key()` (`backlog_core/rendering.py`) collapses every run of non-alphanumeric characters (spaces, literal underscores, any punctuation) to a single `_` with no escaping \u2014 any two distinct display names differing only in which non-alnum characters they used produce the identical key.\\n\\n**Fix classification: needs a design decision, matching this issue's own \\\"Research first\\\" framing.** Two candidate directions: (1) escape literal separator characters before substitution so the reverse transform can distinguish them \u2014 requires a compatibility/migration decision for `unknown__`-prefixed keys already persisted on live GitHub issues; (2) stop deriving the key from a lossy encoding of the display name at all, store the original display name verbatim, and use a different storage key (the same question raised in the related issue #2966 \u2014 worth resolving together per this issue's own note). Touches the encode function, decode function, and both callers that assume the pair round-trips (`operations.py`, `github_sync.py`). Deferring to a design decision rather than auto-fixing.\\n\\n\\n**Related follow-up filed**: #3048 \u2014 a punctuation-triggered variant of this same encoding-collision family found while fixing #2978, distinct reproduction (full render/parse/merge round-trip, not just heading_to_unknown_key), possibly the same design fix as this issue.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"05fe7dd00ed2f0df6d696cfe9a6c63d017ce244dc4e99dfdd7b233c425748d8c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPtXW9w\"}"}